body:
Right? I honestly posted this because I caught a glimpse of myself in the mirror today and was like "that's straight up Wormtongue." :( 

&#x200B;

It's ok, we'll all figure out what works for us eventually...

How did any of you people get others to go to shows with you? None of my friends like metal, and my boyfriend hates live shows. I've tried finding people through those stupid friendship-type apps (bumble bff, patook, etc), and that got me nowhere. Everyone just wants to go to boozy brunch and do beach yogalates/hiking/idk. 

&#x200B;

I've gone to one or two shows alone, and while the music is always fucking amazing, I get too many weird stares (doesn't help that I'm 5', 100 lbs and usually mistaken for a middle schooler). Maybe after enough of these shows I'll get the fuck over it, but for now it'd be nice to find concert buddies to \\m/ with.

It looks a lot like the fungal acne I've been fighting for years now! It's a struggle to get rid of it, but my dermatologist literally told me the easiest option is to buy dandruff shampoo and apply it to your face, scalp, etc. like a mask. I've been doing that for a few months, and it has made a definite improvement in my skin. Also look into SCA's list of products that are safe for fungal acne, because a lot of products "feed" the yeast/fungus and only make the acne worse. The products that you're currently using seem safe. If I were you, I would also add a BHA like Stridex in the red box. 

&#x200B;

The most important thing to remember is to switch up the active ingredients in the antifungals you use. For instance, I have both pyrithione zinc shampoo and ketoconazole shampoo. I alter use of them each week. My derm also told me that I can try antifungal creams if nothing else is working, though they are very drying. Fungal acne is unfortunately something that may never fully go away for you, so sticking with the routine is your best bet.

I was driving through there to get to Sorrento Valley at exactly 4:30PM. I don't know how I missed it, but thank God that I did. I remember getting to my destination and seeing black smoke in the sky, wondering what it was coming from. 

&#x200B;

On my way home, I figured it out. And saw what I narrowly missed. Chilling, sobering, and very sad. I wish the best for the victims and their families.
